#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1074 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "NEW with the M2-P6 ruling (option (b'), Fix #306) - the mirror owed on the FDA side so the byte-identical twin stays identical in BEHAVIOUR as well as in text. FDA-SD1074's Check, Scope, Executability, Description, Outcome.Message and Output_Variables are identical to PMDA-SD1074's; both sheet rows carry the same sentence and the same Domains cell ('ALL'), and neither enumerates anything, so there is no asymmetry to preserve here (unlike M2-P1/P7/P8/P9). Mirror of pmda/PMDA-SD1074/PMDA-SD1074-invalid_agetxt-DM.cdt."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt variable_name=AGETXT
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AGETXT  type=Char label="Age Range"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 18-65
